\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Light, from age to age the same.
\par O ever- living Word,
\par Here have we felt Thy kindling flame,
\par Thy voice within have heard.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Here holy thought and hymn and prayer
\par Have winged the spirit's powers,
\par And made these walls divinely fair,
\par Thy temple, Lord, and ours.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. What visions rise above the years;
\par What tender memories throng,
\par Till the eye fills with happy  tears,
\par The heart with happy song.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Vanish the mists of time and sense;
\par They come, the loved of yore,
\par And one encircling providence
\par Holds all for evermore.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O not in vain their toil, who wrought
\par To build faith's freer shrine;
\par Nor theirs, whose steadfast love and thought
\par Have watched the fire divine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Burn, holy Fire, and shine more wide!
\par While systems rise and fall,
\par Faith, hope, and charity abide,
\par The heart and soul of all.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

